comments[3]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-10-29T20:35:42.930Z","harness:codex","Duplicate check: complete strict all-status corpus3157 with no omissions or unreadable records, request-specific GH-number and semantic searches, current open/in_progress inventories, and full live predecessor data/comments/history. The predecessor scope is delivered; this report names a distinct boundary. New intake is open and unclaimed. Source report: https://github.com/unbraind/pm-cli/issues/1628"
  "2026-10-31T00:26:34.405Z","harness:claude-code","Reproduced on current source (branch base 1a72d089d, built SDK): create closed item, then update(id, {title, status: closed, closeReason: same, force: true}) -> closureChanged=true, clockChanged=true (closed_at 00:17:26.978Z -> 00:17:27.105Z, updated_at -> 00:17:27.110Z). Open-item control with an identical payload: clockChanged=false. Root cause: routeCloseStatusUpdate in src/sdk/lifecycle/update.ts sends any update naming the close status to runClose without checking whether the item is already closed; mutateCloseMetadata then re-stamps closed_at unconditionally and closeItem passes no skipNoop, so item-store stamps updated_at. commitItemMutations reuses update(), so the transaction path shares the defect; update-many already compared before routing and was unaffected."
  "2026-10-31T00:26:34.927Z","harness:claude-code","Fix: routeCloseStatusUpdate now reads the stored item and, when the requested close status, trimmed reason and completed_at already describe it, applies only the remaining fields through the ordinary update path (skipNoop) and reports terminal_state_unchanged; a bare identical update returns changed_fields [] without force. A different reason remains a repeat closure routed to runClose with the existing force gate. After the fix the same repro reports closureChanged=false, clockChanged=false. Negative control: with src/sdk/lifecycle/update.ts stashed, 3 of the 4 new update-command tests fail (changed_fields [status, closed_at, close_reason] vs []); the fourth guards the preserved repeat-closure behaviour and passes both ways. Mixed-batch retry test on commitItemMutations keeps closed_at/updated_at byte-identical across two commits."
